WEBVTT

00:00:04.008 --> 00:00:08.083
CANDY CANDY

00:00:10.814 --> 00:00:16.491
Sobakasu nante kinishinai wa.

00:00:17.310 --> 00:00:23.221
Hana pecha datte datte datte oki ni iri.

00:00:24.231 --> 00:00:27.059
Otenba itazura daisuki,

00:00:27.094 --> 00:00:30.590
Kakekko sukippu daisuki;

00:00:30.625 --> 00:00:35.834
Watashi wa, watashi wa, watashi wa Candy!

00:00:37.366 --> 00:00:43.426
Hitoripocchi de iru to choppiri samishii.

00:00:43.461 --> 00:00:49.904
Sonna toki kou iu no kagami wo mitsumete:

00:00:49.939 --> 00:00:56.287
Waratte, waratte, waratte Candy!

00:00:56.322 --> 00:00:59.174
Nakibeso nante sayonara!

00:00:59.209 --> 00:01:02.527
Nee, Candy Candy!

00:01:13.489 --> 00:01:15.590
Annie is gone.

00:01:16.237 --> 00:01:19.997
Candy's soulmate, with whom she lived
for a whole decade,

00:01:20.032 --> 00:01:24.339
...has gone away to a faraway place,
out of Candy's reach.

00:01:29.114 --> 00:01:34.511
You're cute when you smile!

00:01:40.898 --> 00:01:43.265
Candy!

00:01:44.837 --> 00:01:46.574
Annie!

00:01:47.317 --> 00:01:48.855
Annie!

00:01:50.119 --> 00:01:51.503
Candy!

00:01:53.002 --> 00:01:54.511
Annie!

00:01:58.526 --> 00:01:59.676
Candy!

00:02:01.050 --> 00:02:03.843
Annie, you've come back, right?

00:02:04.772 --> 00:02:05.823
Annie...

00:02:06.287 --> 00:02:07.244
Annie...

00:02:16.928 --> 00:02:18.140
Candy.

00:02:18.772 --> 00:02:19.960
Candy?

00:02:25.488 --> 00:02:27.276
What, was it all a dream?

00:02:27.338 --> 00:02:29.163
You were dreaming about Annie?

00:02:29.629 --> 00:02:31.284
I dreamt that she came back.

00:02:31.319 --> 00:02:33.796
Candy, I'm sure she'll come back!

00:02:34.823 --> 00:02:35.934
Why is that?

00:02:36.567 --> 00:02:41.017
Because I dreamt about me wetting my bed
and it sort of came true.

00:02:41.052 --> 00:02:43.161
You did it again, John?

00:02:58.054 --> 00:03:01.793
I wonder will my dream come true,
just like John said.

00:03:03.598 --> 00:03:05.490
What's the matter, Kurin?

00:03:06.890 --> 00:03:08.438
Is somebody coming?

00:03:15.692 --> 00:03:17.482
Maybe Annie is...

00:03:18.389 --> 00:03:22.221
Oh well... it's Matthew the mailman.

00:03:22.256 --> 00:03:25.133
That's it! He's carrying a letter
from Annie!

00:03:25.582 --> 00:03:26.628
Annie's let- -!

00:03:34.652 --> 00:03:36.814
I sort of fell.

00:03:39.587 --> 00:03:40.929
Mr. Matthew!

00:03:42.105 --> 00:03:44.023
Oh, tomboyish girl from Pony's home!

00:03:44.680 --> 00:03:47.715
Say, have you brought any letters for me?

00:03:47.750 --> 00:03:48.585
For you?

00:03:48.620 --> 00:03:50.160
A letter from Annie!

00:03:50.195 --> 00:03:52.527
I don't know about such a letter.

00:03:53.729 --> 00:03:55.482
Kurin, he doesn't know.

00:04:02.970 --> 00:04:07.107
All of these letters are for sister Pony
and sister Lane...

00:04:08.312 --> 00:04:11.273
Mr. Matthew, maybe your eyesight is going?

00:04:12.402 --> 00:04:13.803
Hey! What are you doing?

00:04:13.838 --> 00:04:15.028
I'm gonna check it myself!

00:04:15.243 --> 00:04:16.249
Wait up!

00:04:20.558 --> 00:04:22.873
-We'll help, too!
-Me too.

00:04:22.908 --> 00:04:23.706
Thanks!

00:04:27.244 --> 00:04:28.371
This one isn't...

00:04:28.406 --> 00:04:30.225
Hey! Return my bag!

00:04:33.009 --> 00:04:34.448
Oh! All these letters...!

00:04:38.913 --> 00:04:40.187
Everyone, help me out!

00:04:45.224 --> 00:04:48.157
-Quickly, catch those goats!
-Okay!

00:04:49.420 --> 00:04:55.235
-Wait!
-Don't do that!

00:05:06.547 --> 00:05:11.133
On the second day...

00:05:22.982 --> 00:05:24.659
Mr. Matthew!

00:05:32.890 --> 00:05:35.355
Welcome, mr. mailman!

00:05:37.475 --> 00:05:40.588
Mr. mailman, welcome!

00:05:40.623 --> 00:05:43.185
Even though you say it like that,
I don't have a letter for Candy.

00:05:43.410 --> 00:05:47.205
Mr. Matthew, you've been delivering
mail for thirty years already?

00:05:48.083 --> 00:05:49.469
And... what if I have?

00:05:49.680 --> 00:05:53.419
And in those thirty years, you've
made an occasional mistake, right?

00:05:54.072 --> 00:05:56.418
I've never done that!

00:05:56.453 --> 00:05:58.917
But... you could be mistaken today!

00:05:59.270 --> 00:06:02.643
I can't just sift through all of my
mail just because you say so!

00:06:02.678 --> 00:06:08.026
There's a regulation preventing
me from showing the mail to anybody.

00:06:08.061 --> 00:06:10.179
Regulation, huh?

00:06:13.844 --> 00:06:20.285
Wha...?
Hey! Don't do that!

00:06:24.862 --> 00:06:27.360
Candy! Others too, cut that out!

00:06:27.395 --> 00:06:29.548
But I was just about done!

00:06:30.484 --> 00:06:33.693
On the third day...

00:06:43.227 --> 00:06:47.851
Oh, there's very little mail today.
I didn't have to bring my bag.

00:06:50.027 --> 00:06:52.914
I'm not carrying anything else with me.

00:06:52.944 --> 00:06:54.700
I guess you're right.

00:07:08.710 --> 00:07:11.584
Gotta stick to the regulations.

00:07:28.423 --> 00:07:29.738
Annie.

00:07:33.026 --> 00:07:36.938
Candy, for how long are you going to keep
thinking about Annie?

00:07:37.673 --> 00:07:38.599
It doesn't suit you, Candy.

00:07:38.832 --> 00:07:42.072
Are you saying that Annie isn't thinking
about me anymore?

00:07:42.247 --> 00:07:46.473
No, I'm sure a letter will arrive from her.

00:07:46.508 --> 00:07:48.998
But... it's already been three days!

00:07:49.033 --> 00:07:51.970
If you can believe in her, you can wait, too.

00:08:03.110 --> 00:08:06.483
Kurin, Annie went down that road.

00:08:10.195 --> 00:08:11.515
Somebody is coming!

00:08:16.202 --> 00:08:19.892
It's okay, Kurin!
But who'd come this late at night?

00:08:44.415 --> 00:08:48.488
Mr. mailman, how come you're wandering around
so late at night? Maybe you got lost?

00:08:53.172 --> 00:08:59.066
What does a mailman do if he gets lost, anyway?
I came just to let you open this bag.

00:08:59.101 --> 00:09:00.135
Let me...?

00:09:00.941 --> 00:09:02.916
Now, open it.

00:09:11.896 --> 00:09:14.279
Is it really okay to open it...?

00:09:15.254 --> 00:09:20.402
Since I came so late at night today,
I'm going to turn a blind eye on regulations.

00:09:32.753 --> 00:09:36.069
Miss Candy...
...Annie Brighton.

00:09:36.499 --> 00:09:39.483
It's Annie!
It's a letter from Annie!

00:09:39.518 --> 00:09:41.224
Thank you, Mr. Matthew!

00:09:41.432 --> 00:09:43.357
Coming so late at night
just to deliver this letter...

00:09:43.392 --> 00:09:48.545
Come on, I just went for an evening walk.
The stars, they are so beautiful.

00:10:01.561 --> 00:10:02.873
Mr. Matthew!

00:10:02.908 --> 00:10:07.736
I thought, if I delivered this letter to
you during the day, you'd burst into tears.

00:10:07.771 --> 00:10:13.551
Crying in front of everybody, you'd
probably feel embarassed.

00:10:13.586 --> 00:10:15.295
I wouldn't!

00:10:17.943 --> 00:10:19.490
I wouldn't cry.

00:10:20.678 --> 00:10:22.490
Good night, Candy.

00:10:30.173 --> 00:10:31.211
Candy?

00:10:33.270 --> 00:10:39.017
That's great, Candy!
Come, you can read it in our room.

00:10:39.184 --> 00:10:40.544
I'll read it here!

00:10:41.911 --> 00:10:43.732
In such a dark place?

00:10:43.767 --> 00:10:46.836
It'll lighten up as soon as I start to read!

00:10:49.025 --> 00:10:50.652
It's not a problem!

00:10:50.687 --> 00:10:52.108
Candy...

00:11:05.226 --> 00:11:08.132
"To my dear friend Candy."

00:11:09.716 --> 00:11:12.385
"I'm so happy now."

00:11:13.084 --> 00:11:16.423
"I'm living in a big house with
a swimming pool and many servants!"

00:11:16.458 --> 00:11:21.342
"My Father and Mother are very gentle,
and living here is almost like in a dream."

00:11:22.181 --> 00:11:27.522
"I'll soon ask Father and Mother to
let me introduce you to them."

00:11:28.521 --> 00:11:30.747
"Until then, keep your spirits up!"

00:11:39.779 --> 00:11:42.273
I'm so glad that Annie is happy!

00:11:42.966 --> 00:11:50.522
*Denjin Anime Fansub*
During the 1970's, even toddlers had sideburns!

00:11:56.352 --> 00:11:57.592
This is today's mail.

00:11:58.320 --> 00:11:59.558
Thank you.

00:12:04.186 --> 00:12:05.560
Mail has just arrived.

00:12:05.967 --> 00:12:07.134
Thank you.

00:12:17.109 --> 00:12:18.123
Come in!

00:12:19.573 --> 00:12:20.573
Excuse me.

00:12:21.171 --> 00:12:23.537
Miss, mail has arrived for you.

00:12:23.727 --> 00:12:24.645
Thank you!

00:12:26.523 --> 00:12:28.434
It's from Candy!

00:12:28.469 --> 00:12:29.500
Hold on, Becky.

00:12:33.560 --> 00:12:35.736
You like chocolate, right?

00:12:35.956 --> 00:12:37.535
Yes. But...

00:12:37.570 --> 00:12:38.778
You don't have to take it.

00:12:39.935 --> 00:12:42.449
Madam, excuse me!

00:12:42.593 --> 00:12:45.861
Annie, Becky is not your friend.

00:12:46.511 --> 00:12:47.978
I understand, Mother...

00:12:50.996 --> 00:12:52.289
It's from Candy, right?

00:12:52.324 --> 00:12:53.033
Yes.

00:12:53.915 --> 00:12:56.366
Pony's home, Candice White.

00:12:57.160 --> 00:13:00.227
Actually, I've been thinking about
this for days.

00:13:00.623 --> 00:13:02.635
What about?

00:13:04.936 --> 00:13:11.852
Heavens know how many people could have looked at
this letter before it reached your hands.

00:13:11.887 --> 00:13:12.514
Yes...

00:13:13.233 --> 00:13:18.312
Nobody took notice of it yet, but it would be
better for you, and for the namesake...

00:13:18.347 --> 00:13:23.457
...of the Brighton family if nobody knew
about this orphanage they call Pony's home.

00:13:24.486 --> 00:13:27.322
What would people say if they knew that
you were raised in a dark swamp?

00:13:27.967 --> 00:13:31.930
Everybody will refer to you as to a child
which is under my protection, understood?

00:13:32.420 --> 00:13:36.586
Be a good girl and don't tell anyone
about this, okay?

00:13:37.012 --> 00:13:38.389
Yes.

00:13:44.270 --> 00:13:47.058
I'll have someong bring in the
goods we just bought in town.

00:13:47.711 --> 00:13:50.088
We'll make a new dress for your party.

00:14:07.983 --> 00:14:09.417
It's a big one!

00:14:13.020 --> 00:14:15.172
-How many do we need?
-Just a little more!

00:14:15.207 --> 00:14:17.180
A letter came from your friend!

00:14:17.585 --> 00:14:19.346
It's from Annie, right, Mr. Matthew?

00:14:24.270 --> 00:14:25.955
Hold on, Kurin.

00:14:29.400 --> 00:14:31.610
It's not the usual gentle Annie.

00:14:32.477 --> 00:14:34.257
"I'm sorry, Candy."

00:14:34.453 --> 00:14:36.932
"I can't write letters to you anymore."

00:14:37.118 --> 00:14:39.263
"So, this is a last letter to you."

00:14:40.226 --> 00:14:42.836
"In order to become a true daughter
of the Brighton family,"

00:14:42.871 --> 00:14:45.843
"I have to forget everything
about Pony's home."

00:14:46.582 --> 00:14:48.614
"Please don't ask me anything."

00:14:52.078 --> 00:14:53.692
What's the meaning of this?

00:15:03.634 --> 00:15:04.816
This is terrible.

00:15:04.851 --> 00:15:06.512
Having to forget everything.

00:15:07.307 --> 00:15:10.045
How could she forget about us
and everyone at this place?

00:15:27.998 --> 00:15:29.980
I can't believe you, Annie.

00:15:30.676 --> 00:15:34.859
Whenever I closed my eyes,
I saw your face...

00:15:35.437 --> 00:15:40.033
And whenever I closed my ears,
I heard your voice, Annie!

00:15:40.721 --> 00:15:42.854
Does it matter if you're
doing so well?!

00:15:44.492 --> 00:15:45.931
Does it matter at all?

00:16:43.484 --> 00:16:45.777
Who are you?

00:16:46.186 --> 00:16:47.479
Whom do I look alike?

00:16:47.514 --> 00:16:49.991
Your clothes are so weird.
You look like an alien!

00:16:50.026 --> 00:16:50.855
An alien?

00:16:51.233 --> 00:16:56.646
Because you're a guy, wearing a skirt...
And you have a flute with a belly...

00:16:56.883 --> 00:17:01.676
It's not a skirt. It's called "kilt";
a Scottish folk costume.

00:17:02.073 --> 00:17:05.619
And this belly-thing is a musical
instrument, called "bagpipes".

00:17:24.441 --> 00:17:27.412
It sounds like snails are having a party!

00:17:29.383 --> 00:17:32.103
Snail party? That's a good one!

00:17:42.487 --> 00:17:46.393
You are prettier when you're smiling
than when you're crying.

00:17:46.428 --> 00:17:48.744
You stood there and watched me cry!

00:17:50.829 --> 00:17:52.077
Oh, my letter...!

00:17:52.732 --> 00:17:53.739
Wait!

00:17:55.266 --> 00:17:56.499
Got it!

00:17:58.263 --> 00:18:01.073
Can you make that snail-like sound
once again?

00:18:04.429 --> 00:18:05.181
Huh?

00:18:11.629 --> 00:18:13.685
Was I dreaming?

00:18:14.358 --> 00:18:17.697
Come to think of it, he did look
a lot like a prince from a fairy tale.

00:18:18.677 --> 00:18:22.257
You are prettier when you're smiling
than when you're crying.

00:18:32.725 --> 00:18:34.372
That's a pretty pendant.

00:18:43.226 --> 00:18:45.054
The Prince must have dropped it.

00:19:14.240 --> 00:19:17.878
Say, have you seen someone carrying
a flute with a belly?

00:19:18.333 --> 00:19:20.814
No...
Are you from Pony's home?

00:19:21.202 --> 00:19:22.012
Yes.

00:19:22.428 --> 00:19:25.806
If that's true, could you
bring her along with yourself?

00:19:26.088 --> 00:19:28.246
Ma'am, she is...?

00:19:28.488 --> 00:19:35.026
I would like to leave her at Pony's home.
I already have more children than I can care for...

00:19:35.342 --> 00:19:36.040
I see...

00:19:36.075 --> 00:19:39.726
I thought about leaving her here and
going off to work...

00:19:40.695 --> 00:19:43.490
Candy! Sister Pony is calling you!

00:19:43.915 --> 00:19:46.248
Well then, ma'am.

00:19:48.248 --> 00:19:49.875
It's incredible!

00:19:53.177 --> 00:19:55.000
Whose automobile is this?

00:19:55.209 --> 00:19:59.576
It's incredible! This is a first
automobile ever to visit Pony's home!

00:20:02.974 --> 00:20:05.062
It looks like that pendant.

00:20:05.281 --> 00:20:07.771
That's it! The prince must have
come with this car.

00:20:08.007 --> 00:20:11.846
This is Mr. Stewart from the Leagan family.

00:20:13.085 --> 00:20:17.107
Mr. Stewart would like to introduce you
into the Leagan family.

00:20:17.296 --> 00:20:19.185
Me?

00:20:19.535 --> 00:20:24.765
Leagan family has built up quite
a reputation in the town of Lakewood.

00:20:25.136 --> 00:20:29.262
Lakewood... this city is close to
Annie.

00:20:29.574 --> 00:20:30.873
Yes, that's correct.

00:20:31.400 --> 00:20:33.596
Can I ask you one thing?

00:20:33.802 --> 00:20:35.776
Go ahead.

00:20:38.988 --> 00:20:43.083
Is there a seventeen or eighteen year
old boy in your family?

00:20:43.700 --> 00:20:46.590
Yes, there is. Family's son.

00:20:51.336 --> 00:20:54.852
Sister Pony, I'm off to Lakewood!

00:20:54.914 --> 00:20:55.846
Huh?

00:20:56.969 --> 00:20:59.128
I'm going to become a member of
the Leagan family.

00:20:59.346 --> 00:21:02.449
Candy! How come that you've so
suddenly...

00:21:02.646 --> 00:21:04.193
Thank you very much.

00:21:07.202 --> 00:21:09.124
Wait up, Candy!

00:21:23.000 --> 00:21:23.936
Ma'am!

00:21:26.553 --> 00:21:28.740
I made it in time!

00:21:30.825 --> 00:21:33.600
From today, you'll live
in Pony's home.

00:21:37.154 --> 00:21:38.595
Uh...

00:21:38.805 --> 00:21:42.326
There is one happy girl who is
leaving Pony's home now.

00:21:42.361 --> 00:21:44.976
Therefore, you can take her
place in Pony's home.

00:21:45.691 --> 00:21:46.948
Really?

00:21:47.560 --> 00:21:50.785
Yes. She just made up her mind.

00:21:50.820 --> 00:21:55.910
She is going to become a
richest young lady in Lakewood.

00:21:56.171 --> 00:21:58.207
Oh, my...

00:22:00.699 --> 00:22:05.958
And her best friend is just
near Lakewood.

00:22:06.750 --> 00:22:08.548
Could someone possibly be
any happier than her?

00:22:08.735 --> 00:22:10.887
Isn't that girl called...

00:22:11.292 --> 00:22:12.966
Candice White.

00:22:13.370 --> 00:22:16.735
Actually, that's my name.
It's me.

00:22:18.966 --> 00:22:25.758
To meet Annie... to meet the Prince...
From now on, she will live in happiness.

00:22:25.793 --> 00:22:31.376
Tears of joy kept rolling down Candy's face.

00:22:31.411 --> 00:22:33.915
To be continued.

00:22:40.400 --> 00:22:48.892
Ashita wa doko kara
umarete kuru no

00:22:49.265 --> 00:22:58.683
Watashi wa, ashita ga,
ashita ga suki.

00:22:59.032 --> 00:23:07.801
Suteki na koto ga
ari sore

00:23:08.010 --> 00:23:17.284
Watashi wa, ashita ga
ashita ga suki.

00:23:17.693 --> 00:23:26.015
Kirakira hikaru
Kaze no mukou de

00:23:26.191 --> 00:23:37.096
Ano hito ga watashi wo
Watashi wo yondeiru - -

00:23:37.483 --> 00:23:48.566
Candy, Candy, Candy, Candy.

00:23:49.219 --> 00:23:52.403
Next episode:
From today, I'll be a princess?

00:23:52.621 --> 00:23:55.959
Finally, I've left Pony's home.

00:23:56.673 --> 00:24:00.290
It was incredibly hard to part from
sisters and all of my little friends.

00:24:01.085 --> 00:24:05.498
But knowing that Tom and Annie are living
in happiness, I'll put up with anything!

00:24:06.342 --> 00:24:10.898
I'm going to live at a huge Leagan's
residence in Lakewood!

00:24:11.118 --> 00:24:13.060
I wonder what kind of people are they.

00:24:13.308 --> 00:24:16.537
Next time on "Candy Candy",
"From today, I'll be a princess?"

00:24:16.732 --> 00:24:19.266
See you again!
